  "question": {
    "text": "The de-Broglie wavelength $(\\lambda)$ for electron (e), proton $(p)$ and $\\mathrm{He}^{2+}$ ion $(\\alpha)$ are in the following order. (Speed of e, p and $\\alpha$ are the same)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ay67p",
      "text": "$\\alpha>p>e$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1rWxy",
      "text": "$e>p>\\alpha$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "mH53Y",
      "text": "$e>\\alpha>p$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hzVLk",
      "text": "$\\alpha < p>e$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\lambda=\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{\\mathrm{mv}}$\n$\\because$ speed are same\n$\\begin{aligned}\n&\\therefore \\lambda \\propto \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~m}} \\\\\n&\\therefore \\lambda_e>\\lambda_p>\\lambda_\\alpha \\text { as } \\quad \\mathrm{m}_\\alpha>\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{p}}>\\mathrm{m}_e\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
